# SHA256 manifest for the pinned Qwen 3.8 27B 4-bit target.
# Revision: eda45ab47f465d08d6558f0353a2346e2eb9d5b3
# Format: <sha256> <byte_count> <relative_path>
#
# GENERATED FROM THE PUBLISHED SNAPSHOT 2026-08-14. This file was a header-only
# stub from the identity swap until the upload landed; the body below is
# generated alongside the digests it has to agree with, from the published
# revision named above, which is what the stub's own note required.
#
# The backbone reference checkpoint is OUR OWN mlx-0.32.0 conversion (MLX 4-bit
# affine, group_size 64) of the official bf16 base Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B @
# 1d4bf0f2ff6012fd82039f2fa52739d0dd7c60c0. The shard split is three
# safetensors files, which is a property of our toolchain and was measured at
# publish rather than assumed.
#
# THE SHAPE PINS MOVE WITH THIS BODY, in this commit, because a count that is
# not summed from the digests it must agree with is not a pin:
#
#   MLXFAST_QWEN_MTP_TARGET_MANIFEST_RECORDS: 10
#   MLXFAST_QWEN_MTP_TARGET_MANIFEST_BYTES:   15153237117
#
# and so do the contract fixture's target.manifest_sha256 and
# target.expected_source_bytes.
#
# RECORD SCOPE -- RESOLVED 2026-08-22 by operator ruling: KEEP THE TEN
# LOAD-BEARING RECORDS. The published repository carries an ELEVENTH file, the
# `.gitattributes` Hugging Face generates for every repo
# (34448b82c17d60fec9b65b1f093c115ddbaadc04beb1b0140b6bfed2e012a930, 1570
# bytes). It is DELIBERATELY NOT pinned, and the two shape pins stay at
# 10 / 15153237117: `.gitattributes` is never engine-loaded, the per-shard
# digests above are the real defense, and tree-equality over generated platform
# metadata is purity, not protection. `verify_cache` verifies these ten
# load-bearing records' pins and IGNORES non-loaded platform metadata -- it does
# not require the cache tree to equal the manifest over a file nothing loads. A
# stock `snapshot_download` of this revision therefore stages one unpinned,
# unloaded `.gitattributes` alongside the ten pinned files, which is fine; do
# NOT add an eleventh record to move the pins to 11 / 15153238687. (Run
# 31665285024 died on the old strict-inventory-in-both-directions posture; the
# fix is this load-bearing scope, not pinning the generated platform file.)
#
# WHAT THIS FILE NAMED BEFORE, and why it moved. On 2026-08-14 these header
# lines named a third-party personal-account conversion of the same bf16 base,
# adopted that morning. The adoption was TERMINATED the same day by the
# operator's validation kill-switch: the deterministic reconversion cross-check
# it had reserved was performed, and 994 of 1,847 tensors differ numerically
# from our own conversion. The upstream bf16 base did not move and is the
# lineage the records below descend from.
#
# THE 3.6 RECORDS WERE DELETED RATHER THAN CARRIED, one commit before this one:
# a manifest of 3.6 bytes checked against a 3.8 cache directory reports every
# file missing and reads as a corrupt download rather than as an unfinished
# pin. The stub window that reasoning opened is now closed by real records.
#
# THE TOWER, for readers who come here for it: 1,847 tensors, every one of them
# under the `language_model.` prefix and NONE under `mtp.`. The MTP head ships
# separately -- see fixtures/qwen3_8_27b_mtp_head.sha256 -- exactly as it did
# on 3.6.
